TITLE:: RCSurface
summary:: A parametric surface in R^m, sampled for its tangent lines, rulings and the curves on it
categories:: Libraries>reCurrent
related:: Classes/RCLines, Classes/RCProjection

DESCRIPTION::
A surface is a Function (u, v) → Array of strong::dim:: numbers over uRange × vRange. link::Classes/RCLines#*projected:: samples it (link::#-grid::, link::#-random::, link::#-walk::), takes a tangent segment, the v-line (the ruling) or a curve on the surface through each sample and projects it on a score space with an link::Classes/RCProjection::. The presets are the surfaces Xenakis drew for Metastasis and the Philips Pavilion (ruled: the cone, the conoid, the hyperbolic paraboloid, the hyperboloid of one sheet), the surface ruled by two rails, the surface of the tangents of a curve, and closed surfaces for projected textures (sphere, torus, the Clifford torus in R^4). Rulings run along v where a preset is ruled.

The curves on a surface are integrated in the parameters by Runge-Kutta 4, their equations written in R^m with the metric of the first partials (link::#-metric::), so they work in any dimension: link::#-geodesic:: (the straightest curves: a ruling, a great circle; its acceleration in R^m has no part along the surface), link::#-paramLine::, and link::#-flow::, the steepest ascent of a time function (a projection's time, or any Function of R^m): at unit time, the strands of a section of the surface by a moving hyperplane. A function on the patch has level sets (link::#-levelSet::, marching squares) and critical points (link::#-criticalPoints::: where strands are born, part and converge). The curves read the second partials at every step: the presets give them (link::#-secondPartials::), other surfaces take differences of the first. Costs measured in sclang: a geodesic of 12 steps about 1 ms with its projection (1.4 ms in R^4), a 32 × 32 level set 6 ms, critical points 15 ms.

CLASSMETHODS::

METHOD:: new
argument:: func
(u, v) → Array of dim numbers.
argument:: dim
argument:: uRange
argument:: vRange
argument:: du
argument:: dv
Partial derivatives, Functions (u, v) → Array; central differences (link::#-eps::) when nil.
argument:: name

subsection:: Presets
METHOD:: plane
code::[u, v, 0]::.
METHOD:: hyperbolicParaboloid
code::[u, v, u v / c]::, doubly ruled: the string section of Metastasis, the Pavilion's walls.
METHOD:: conoid
The right conoid (helicoid) code::[v cos u, v sin u, c u]::, rulings through the axis.
METHOD:: cone
code::[v cos u, v sin u, v]::: the fan.
METHOD:: cylinder
METHOD:: hyperboloid
One sheet, code::[cos u - v sin u, sin u + v cos u, v]::, the v-lines straight.
METHOD:: sphere
u the azimuth, v the elevation.
METHOD:: torus
argument:: bigR
argument:: r
METHOD:: clifford
The Clifford torus in R^4, code::[cos u, sin u, cos v, sin v] / sqrt 2::: flat, and every rotation of R^4 shows it differently to a projection.
METHOD:: rails
S(u, v) = A(u) + v (B(u) - A(u)) for two Functions u → Array: the strings between two rails. With strong::via:: (a third rail u → Array) the v-lines are quadratic Bézier arcs pulled towards it, code::Q = mid + 2 pull (M - mid)::: strong::pull:: 0 the ruled surface, 1 the arcs through M at their middle (a generalized ruled surface, its generatrices curved), its v derivative analytic.
argument:: a
argument:: b
argument:: dim
argument:: uRange
argument:: vRange
argument:: via
argument:: pull
METHOD:: tangentDevelopable
S(u, v) = C(u) + v C'(u) for a curve C (a Function u → Array): ruled by the tangents of the curve, the Xenakeur construction as a surface.

INSTANCEMETHODS::

METHOD:: at
The point at (u, v).
METHOD:: du
METHOD:: dv
The partial derivatives at (u, v).
METHOD:: duu
METHOD:: duv
METHOD:: dvv
The second partials at (u, v): from the Functions given to link::#-secondPartials::, else central differences of the first partials.
METHOD:: secondPartials
Give the second partials as Functions (u, v) → Array of dim numbers (nil: differences). Returns the surface.
argument:: duu
argument:: duv
argument:: dvv
METHOD:: tangent
code::cos(angle) * du + sin(angle) * dv::.
METHOD:: normal
The unit normal (dim 3 only), nil elsewhere or where the tangents are dependent.
METHOD:: metric
The first fundamental form at (u, v): code::[E, F, G]::, the dot products of the partials.
METHOD:: contains
Whether (u, v) lies on the patch (a periodic parameter always does).

subsection:: Curves on the surface
Samples code::[u, v]::, unwrapped across a periodic seam (the surface is evaluated there as it is). A curve stops at the edge of a patch that is not periodic and at a singular point (where the partials are dependent: a pole, an apex).
METHOD:: geodesic
The geodesic leaving (u, v) along code::cos(angle) S_u + sin(angle) S_v::, strong::length:: long in R^m (negative: the other way), in strong::steps:: steps. nil where the direction vanishes.
argument:: u
argument:: v
argument:: angle
argument:: length
argument:: steps
METHOD:: geodesicAccel
The parameter acceleration code::[u'', v'']:: of a geodesic through (u, v) at the parameter velocity (up, vp), nil at a singular point.
METHOD:: paramLine
The parameter line through (u, v), along u (strong::which:: code::\u::) or v (code::\v::), strong::length:: long in R^m (its arc length; negative: backwards).
METHOD:: flow
The steepest ascent through (u, v) of a time function, strong::timeFunc:: (an link::Classes/RCProjection::: its time; or a Function, a point of R^m → number), in strong::steps:: steps; a negative strong::length:: descends. With strong::unit:: code::\time:: its time grows by one per unit of length (length in time units: the strands of a section ride it), with code::\length:: at unit speed in R^m. A step whose time does not grow as it should (at unit time by half to five quarters of the step: Runge-Kutta overshoots where the flow runs ever faster, nearing a critical point) is tried again at half the length, four times; then it stops: at a top, where strands converge (a bottom, going down), at a saddle reached along its separatrix. Returns code::[time, u, v]:: samples, each with the time of its point.
METHOD:: timeAt
The time function at (u, v).
METHOD:: surfaceGradient
The time function's gradient along the surface at (u, v) in parameters (code::g⁻¹ ∇τ::) with its squared length: code::[[u', v'], |∇_S T|²]::, nil at a singular point.

subsection:: Functions on the patch
A Function (u, v) → number, on a grid of nu × nv nodes (link::#-grid::'s, wrapped where periodic).
METHOD:: levelSet
The level set code::{func(u, v) = value}:: by marching squares (a saddle cell decided by its centre): an Array of polylines of code::[u, v]::, each in order along the curve and unwrapped across a periodic seam (a closed one ends on its first point, or a period on when it goes round).
argument:: func
argument:: value
argument:: nu
argument:: nv
METHOD:: criticalPoints
The critical points of func: Events code::(u:, v:, value:, kind:):: with kind code::\min::, code::\max:: (a node below or above all its neighbours) or code::\saddle:: (the neighbours' signs, relative to it, change four times or more around it). An interior one is moved to the stationary point of the quadratic through its neighbours; on the border of a patch that is not periodic, only the extremes of what is there. Nodes on one point of R^m (a pole) count once.
argument:: func
argument:: nu
argument:: nv
METHOD:: grid
nu × nv samples code::[u, v]:: over the ranges, the ends included unless the parameter is periodic.
METHOD:: random
n samples uniform over the ranges, seeded.
METHOD:: walk
A random walk of n samples from strong::start:: (the ranges' middle by default), wrapped over a periodic range, clipped otherwise; seeded.
METHOD:: uPeriodic
METHOD:: vPeriodic
Whether a parameter wraps (set by the presets).
METHOD:: eps
The step of the central differences.
METHOD:: dim
METHOD:: uRange
METHOD:: vRange
METHOD:: name

EXAMPLES::
code::
~s = RCSurface.torus(2, 0.7);
~s.at(1, 2);
~s.normal(1, 2);
~s.grid(8, 4).size;   // 32
~s.walk(16, 0.3, 0.3, seed: 1);

// curves on it
~s.geodesic(0, 0.5, 0.3pi, 4);                          // 4 long in R^3: samples [u, v]
~p = RCProjection(3, [\pitch]);                          // time = x
~s.flow(0.5pi, 0.3, ~p, 2);                              // [time, u, v], one unit of time per unit
~s.levelSet({ |u, v| ~s.timeAt(u, v, ~p) }, 1);          // where the hyperplane x = 1 cuts it
~s.criticalPoints({ |u, v| ~s.timeAt(u, v, ~p) });       // its top, bottom and two saddles
::
